==============================================================================
  tgic_v3 self-tests: {'golay_filter': True, 'three_six_nine': True, 'relational_simulator': True, 'validation': True}
  Golay layer: codewords=4096 octads=759 weights={0: 1, 8: 759, 12: 2576, 16: 759, 24: 1}

  metric                          primes  composites
  axis score (3)                0.536182    0.540989
  face score (6)                0.721295    0.757219
  stability                     0.663450    0.680540
  face vectors left un-snapped (not codewords): 0/30 primes, 9/30 composites
  v3 changes that matter:
    * the 9-neighbour rule no longer counts the node itself (v6.2 did);
    * faces are snapped only when the decoder certifies the result,
      which is honest but still leaves face vectors off-code (9/60 here);
      v6.2 instead re-encoded the information half, which always gives
      a codeword but can move the state by up to 12 bits.
    * with the complete decoder of lattice_shortcut.py both problems
      disappear: every face vector is the nearest codeword, <= 4 bits away.

